      "evidence": [
        "delegation/SKILL.md § Scope: 'This Skill operates delegation directly through the current harness … It does not own domain truth, semantic acceptance, provider choice, concurrency policy, retry policy, or durable execution state.'",
        "delegation/SKILL.md § Completion standard: 'Delegation is complete when the whole remains owned, every contribution has a bounded role and effect surface, returned claims are traceable, conflicts and unknowns are reconstructed rather than voted away, appropriate verification has occurred, and no sub-agent result silently gained human or project acceptance authority.'",
        "delegation/delegation.md § Compressed return and reconstruction: 'Main reconstructs results with an obligation map, checks common source revision and effect ownership, inspects the shared diff or artifacts, and runs the integration or behavior checks appropriate to the whole.'"
      ],
      "consequence": "The Main Agent constructs the delegation envelopes, embeds the worker/reviewer contracts, releases through the active harness, steers without duplicating ownership, and reconnects evidence to the whole. The durable Rossovia obligation remains truthful because the Main Agent never delegates acceptance authority."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The delegation mechanism (envelope, topology, steering) is separate from optional persistence (Rossovia task state).",
      "evidence": [
        "delegation/AGENTS.md § Separate mechanism, adapter, and policy: 'the mechanism owns invariant control flow and evidence, an adapter owns one external system's protocol and error semantics, and policy owns today's ordering, defaults, credentials, budgets, and product choice.'",
        "delegation/SKILL.md § Boundaries: 'Runtime mechanics such as capacity, cancellation, retry, persistence, and recovery remain properties of the active harness.'"
      ],
      "consequence": "The operating topology (parallel investigators + reviewer) is the mechanism. The Rossovia durable task is a separate policy/adapter concern that records the obligation; it does not drive the delegation flow. The Main Agent can execute the work now without waiting for the Rossovia writer."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The Main Agent withholds authority to accept, merge, publish, or redefine the shared contract.",
      "evidence": [
        "delegation/delegation.md § Reviewer envelope: 'Authority withheld: no implementation, acceptance, merge, or publication'.",
        "delegation/delegation.md § Delegation envelope: 'Authority withheld' is a required field for every worker."
      ],
      "consequence": "Workers and reviewer are explicitly forbidden from accepting the final comparison. The Main Agent retains that authority and will later hand the verified capability note to the designated writer."
    }
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "Whether the active harness can isolate the reviewer's context from the producer's conversation history (delegation/delegation.md § Reviewer envelope). If not, the review must be recorded as correlated, not independent.",
    "The exact acceptance contract for the comparison (the 'capability note' criteria) is not yet defined in the supplied sources; the Main Agent must obtain it before contracting the reviewer."
  ],
  "recommendedNextStep": "Main Agent: (1) obtain the exact acceptance contract for the capability note; (2) construct two parallel investigation envelopes using the delegation.md envelope template, each with one provider spec, read-only boundary, and embedded worker.md contract; (3) release both through the active harness; (4) on return, construct a reviewer envelope with the two claims, acceptance contract, and embedded reviewer.md contract; (5) release the reviewer; (6) reconstruct the obligation map, verify against authoritative sources, and retain the final verified comparison for the Rossovia writer."
}

